ernium similar to  what's used in shampoos to detangle and  add volume you might see natural oils  like coconut and argan oil these tend to  form thicker films on hair and this  really weighs it down and so usually  they're used at low concentrations and  conditioners you might also have  hydrolyzed proteins and amino acids  these can penetrate into the hair a bit  and add strength by plugging holes in  the hair i was actually quite surprised  by how well this worked on my hair if  you followed my hair bleaching journey  you'll know that i pretty much need  specialized silicones like emo  dimethicone to make my hair not be straw  this conditioner detangled my hair  really nicely when i was washing it and  it felt nice for about a day  but by day two my hair started feeling a  bit dry i think this would have been  fantastic for my hair before i bleached  it but now i need those extra damaged  coating ingredients so i would recommend  trying this if your hair is not quite  this level of damaged if you want a  conditioner that doesn't weigh your hair  down or if you want something fragrance  free again there really aren't that many  options for fragrance-free hair  conditioners so i'm really happy to see  this as an option for people who want it  i hope you enjoyed this deep dive into  shampoos and conditioners let me know if  you're interested in other product  breakdowns make sure you like and  subscribe links to the ordinary's hair  products are in the description more  videos about cosmetic science are  popping up around me now
 

